.TH CMDBEEPER 1 "August 2026" "cmdbeeper 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cmdbeeper \- beep repeatedly until Enter is pressed or a timer elapses
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cmdbeeper
.RB [ \-s
.IR sound_file ]
.RB [ \-i
.IR interval ]
.RB [ \-t
.IR timeout ]
.RB [ \-e ]
.RB [ \-v | \-q ]
.br
.B cmdbeeper
.B \-h
.br
.B cmdbeeper
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cmdbeeper
plays a sound repeatedly, once per interval, until the user presses
Enter or an optional timeout is reached. It is intended to be chained
after a long-running command as an audible completion notification:
.PP
.RS
$ ./slow_build.sh; cmdbeeper
.RE
.PP
Playback and cleanup are signal-safe: pressing Ctrl-C, or sending
.B SIGINT
or
.B SIGTERM
to the process, stops the current sound immediately and exits cleanly
rather than waiting for the clip in progress to finish.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-s " sound_file"
Path to the audio file to play, passed to
.BR paplay (1).
Defaults to
.I /usr/share/sounds/freedesktop/stereo/alarm-clock-elapsed.oga
or the value of
.BR CMDBEEPER_TUNE ,
if set.
.TP
.BI \-i " interval"
Seconds to wait between repetitions. Must be a non-negative integer.
Defaults to
.B 0
(no gap between repetitions) or the value of
.BR CMDBEEPER_INTERVAL ,
if set.
.TP
.BI \-t " timeout"
Stop automatically after
.I timeout
seconds even if Enter is never pressed. Must be a non-negative
integer. Overrides
.BR CMDBEEPER_TIMER ,
if set. Incompatible with
.BR \-e .
.TP
.B \-e
Run with no timeout, ignoring any timeout inherited from
.BR CMDBEEPER_TIMER .
Incompatible with
.BR \-t .
.TP
.B \-v
Show the "Press Enter to stop..." prompt even if
.B CMDBEEPER_QUIET
is set in the environment. Incompatible with
.BR \-q .
.TP
.B \-q
Suppress the "Press Enter to stop..." prompt. Incompatible with
.BR \-v .
.TP
.B \-h
Show a brief usage message and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version and license information and exit. Must be given as the
only argument.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CMDBEEPER_TUNE
Overrides the default sound file. Equivalent to
.BR \-s .
.TP
.B CMDBEEPER_INTERVAL
Overrides the default interval, in seconds. Equivalent to
.BR \-i .
.TP
.B CMDBEEPER_TIMER
Sets a default timeout, in seconds. Equivalent to
.BR \-t .
Cleared by
.BR \-e .
.TP
.B CMDBEEPER_QUIET
If set to any value, suppresses the "Press Enter to stop..." prompt
by default. Equivalent to
.BR \-q .
Cleared by
.BR \-v .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Stopped normally, either by Enter or by the timeout elapsing.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid or conflicting command-line options, or an invalid
.B CMDBEEPER_INTERVAL
/
.B CMDBEEPER_TIMER
value.
.PP
If the sound backend fails (for example,
.BR paplay (1)
cannot find or read the sound file), cmdbeeper stops the beep loop and
exits with
.BR paplay 's
own exit status, rather than looping indefinitely on a failing command.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Beep after a long build, using the default sound and interval:
.B make; cmdbeeper
.TP
Run a makeshift alarm that goes off after 60 seconds:
.B sleep 60; cmdbeeper
.TP
Beep every 2 seconds using a custom sound, for at most 60 seconds:
.B cmdbeeper -s ~/sounds/ding.oga -i 2 -t 60
.TP
Run quietly (no on-screen prompt), overriding an inherited default:
.B cmdbeeper -q
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR paplay (1)
